menu "HTTP server manager"

    config HTTP_SERVER_MANAGER_STACK_PSRAM
        bool "Run the HTTP server task on a PSRAM stack"
        default y
        # IDF 6: the option that lets a task stack live in PSRAM is
        # FREERTOS_TASK_CREATE_ALLOW_EXT_MEM (SPIRAM_ALLOW_STACK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY
        # is its deprecated spelling and no longer a symbol)
        depends on FREERTOS_TASK_CREATE_ALLOW_EXT_MEM
        help
            The HTTP server task's 12 KB stack is allocated from PSRAM
            (esp_http_server's task_caps) instead of 8 KB of internal RAM.
            Every flash access a route handler makes (the settings files,
            the NVS records, an OTA upload, a /data stream) runs through
            the flash_jobs worker, so nothing on this task runs with the
            flash cache off. Switch off for a build that must keep the
            server's stack internal (then 8 KB, the 2026-09-22 size).

endmenu
